# NestedText v3 - docbook/5.1 schematron DETAIL pass (measured 2026-09-16)
# Source: cc-resources/.dtd-file-examples/docbook/5.1/sch/ (4 files, script census).
# Second of the what-is-not-yet-transmigrated remainder: the 5.1 rule set.

rule-census:
    docbookxi.sch: 15 patterns, 83 asserts
    docbook.sch: 15 patterns, 83 asserts
    dbits.sch: 15 patterns, 83 asserts
    assembly.sch: 16 patterns, 85 asserts

exclusion-matrices:
    > Admonitions never nest: caution important note tip warning exclude
    > each other in all five contexts, 25 asserts for one rule. Caption,
    > equation, example, figure and table exclude each other mutually.
    > Footnote excludes twelve block kinds. The DTD allows the nesting;
    > the schematron refuses it: co-occurrence lives outside the DTD.

linkend-type-constraints:
    > footnoteref points at footnote, firstterm glossterm glosssee and
    > seealso at glossentry, synopfragmentref at synopfragment, indexterm
    > startref at startofrange: reference targets typed by assertion,
    > because IDREF alone cannot say what kind the target is.

xlink-placement:
    > Arc, locator and resource occur only as direct children of extended;
    > extended never nests in extended; title nests in extended, locator
    > or arc. Placement is rank, stated as parent tests.

release-binding:
    > Stream 19 (convergence): the exclusion matrix is where DTD
    > convergence STOPS and the second instrument starts; the suite
    > already has it and calls it checker/. Name that line in the
    > release, per the ceiling-of-a-DTD mechanism, rather than meet it
    > at 11.0.0.
